\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell reported that he hosted an informational table at last week\rquote s Farmers Market, where he provided home organic buckets, answered residents\rquote  questions, and distributed 12 home organic pails.\line\line Library Manager Cassandra Sargent invited the community to an author visit and storytelling event for Otto Normal\rquote s Monsterton on Saturday, March 14, 2026, from 11:00 AM to 12:00 PM; and also announced that the library will participate in the Manhattan Beach Chamber of Commerce\rquote s Ready, Set, Grow event on Sunday, March 15, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 12:00 PM.\line\line City Engineer Gilbert Gamboa invited the community to the groundbreaking ceremony for the 28th Street Storm Drain Infiltration Project, to be held at the northeast corner of Manhattan Avenue and 26th Street on Thursday, March 5, 2026, at 11:00 AM; and also announced a community meeting at the Joslyn Community Center on March 19, 2026, from 7:30 PM to 8:30 PM, where staff will review the construction schedule, discuss anticipated impacts, and answer questions from residents.\line\line Grades of Green Co-founder Lisa Coppedge provided comments regarding the proposed Community Tree Planting Event in honor of Earth Day and Arbor Day.\line\line Mayor Pro Tem Franklin thanked the American Martyrs fifth-grade class for creating the handmade cards for the City Council; and announced a battery recall for Rad Power Bikes with model numbers RP-1304 and HL-RP-S1304, noting that the recalled batteries may pose a fire risk while charging.\line\line Mayor Lesser thanked the American Martyrs fifth-grade class for the personalized cards, noting that they were much appreciated; and invited the community to attend Coffee with the Mayor at Metlox Plaza on Friday, March 6, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


