1.. Presentation of a Proclamation Declaring March 2026, as International Long COVID Awareness Month.
PROCLAIM {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\kerning2\i\f0\fs22 Dr. Elham Raker \kerning0 stated\kerning2  that Long COVID is difficult to measure due to under-diagnosis and includes symptoms such as fatigue, cognitive challenges, and\kerning0  Postural Orthostatic Tachycardia\kerning2  \kerning0 (\kerning2 POTS\kerning0 )\kerning2 . These issues are contributing to student absences and increased accommodation needs. She also mentioned that pediatric long COVID clinics are limited and ongoing attention to the topic is needed.\cf1\kerning0\i0\line\line\cf0\i On behalf of the City Council, Mayor Lesser presented a Proclamation declaring March 2026 as International Long COVID Awareness Month. \cf2\i0\f1\par
}


